# GNU-built Emacs Android APK pins.
#
# Format (one pin per line, parsed by scripts/extract-gnu-apk.sh):
#
#   <sha256>  <api>  <abi>  <emacs-version>
#
# The APKs are fetched from the official GNU mirror (override with
# EMACSHELL_GNU_MIRROR, e.g. https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/emacs/android) as:
#
#   <mirror>/emacs-<version>-<api>-<abi>.apk
#
# Authenticity: each APK has a detached OpenPGP signature at the same URL
# with the ".sig" suffix, signed with the GNU Emacs release key committed
# under keys/emacs-release-key.asc
# (primary fingerprint 6B67 8974 F883 1317 51B2 B1A0 9EF0 C7D0 EDB0 AF5A,
#  "Po Lu <luangruo@yahoo.com>").  GPG verification is performed in CI;
# see .github/workflows/build.yml and SECURITY.md for the trust path.
#
# API levels (from the GNU mirror listing, verified 2026-11-15):
#   arm64-v8a:  api 21, 29, 35     x86_64: api 21, 29, 35
#   armeabi-v7a: api 16, 24
#
# The number in each file name is the MINIMUM API level the package is
# configured for (GNU announcement, Aug 2026): "locate the package
# compiled for its architecture and the nearest API level not exceeding
# that of the operating system".  Two arm64 pins are therefore carried:
#
#   31.1-29  Android 10+ (API 29+); the default build.
#   31.1-21  Android 9 and older (down to the Termux floor, API 24).
#             Subprocesses work on Android <= 9 (the W^X exec
#             restriction arrived in Android 10, which is exactly why
#             the -29 build exists for newer systems).
#
# Which build to assemble is selected with -PgnuApkApi=29|21 (default
# 29); minSdk, versionCode and the APK file name follow it.  The -35
# builds are aligned for 16 KiB pages and needed for devices that ship
# with 16 KiB kernels; tracked in REVIEW.org.

0d44703d92cc5023ed8e9530d8f29ee3a04e5d2d2cc5d7610036446b29e86a2a  29  arm64-v8a  31.1
60eb7ff3477b28542417925c8949e016fe93a3686b38f49a3df886c7ec19f61c  21  arm64-v8a  31.1
